.TH TUI_SGRVIEW_INIT 3 2026-11-15 "libtuikit 1.3" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_sgrview_init, tui_sgrview_free, tui_sgrview_set_text,
tui_sgrview_lines, tui_sgrview_top, tui_sgrview_scroll,
tui_sgrview_scroll_to, tui_sgrview_scroll_end, tui_sgrview_handle,
tui_sgrview_render \- scrolling text that carries SGR styles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/sgrview.h>
.PP
.BI "void tui_sgrview_init(tui_sgrview *" sv );
.BI "void tui_sgrview_free(tui_sgrview *" sv );
.BI "int  tui_sgrview_set_text(tui_sgrview *" sv ", const char *" text );
.BI "int  tui_sgrview_lines(const tui_sgrview *" sv );
.BI "int  tui_sgrview_top(const tui_sgrview *" sv );
.BI "void tui_sgrview_scroll(tui_sgrview *" sv ", int " delta );
.BI "void tui_sgrview_scroll_to(tui_sgrview *" sv ", int " line );
.BI "void tui_sgrview_scroll_end(tui_sgrview *" sv );
.BI "int  tui_sgrview_handle(tui_sgrview *" sv ", const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "void tui_sgrview_render(tui_sgrview *" sv ", tui_canvas " c ", tui_style " st );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The SGR view is
.BR tui_textview_init (3)
for text that carries ANSI SGR sequences
.RB ( ESC\ [ ...\  m ):
a mail body with bold, italic, underline, strike-through and colour.
The sequences are styles, not characters: they take no column, the style in
force at the start of every wrapped line is remembered, so a styled run keeps
its style across a wrap and a scroll, and the cells are drawn through
.BR tui_canvas_put (3)
with a
.IR tui_style .
The view keeps its own copy of the text.
.PP
.BR tui_sgrview_set_text ()
replaces the text and scrolls to the top.
.BR tui_sgrview_render ()
wraps the text to the canvas width if the text or the width changed, clears
the canvas with
.IR st ,
and draws the visible lines.
The styles of the text are laid over
.IR st :
a colour the text sets replaces the one of
.IR st ,
a colour it leaves (default) keeps it, and the attributes add to those of
.IR st .
.SS Sequences understood
0 (reset), 1 bold, 2 dim, 3 italic, 4 underline, 5 and 6 blink, 7 reverse,
9 strike-through, 22 to 25, 27 and 29 (their offs), the colours 30\-37,
90\-97 (foreground) and 40\-47, 100\-107 (background), 38 and 48 with
.B 5;n
(256 colours) or
.B 2;r;g;b
(24-bit; ':' works as the separator too), 39 and 49 (default colour).
Other codes are ignored; other CSI sequences are dropped; a sequence
cut short by the end of the text is dropped.
.SS Wrapping
Lines break at spaces where they can and inside a word where they must; a
wide character is never split; a tab advances to the next multiple of eight
columns; CR before LF is dropped; other control characters are drawn as
U+00B7.
A style carries over a newline.
When the text is longer than the canvas, the last column is a scroll bar
(roles
.B scrollbar.track
and
.BR scrollbar.thumb ),
and the text is one column narrower only while the bar is shown.
.PP
.BR tui_sgrview_handle ()
applies Up, Down, PgUp, PgDn (the rows less two, at least one: two lines overlap), Home and End, and the
shared letters
.RB ( j ", " k ", " ctrl\-f ", " ctrl\-b ", " g ", " G ),
and returns 1 for them; Esc,
.B q
and Backspace are the program's.
.BR tui_sgrview_lines ()
is the number of lines at the last render width.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR tui_sgrview_set_text ()
returns 0, or \-1 with
.I errno
.RB ( EINVAL ,
.BR ENOMEM ;
the old text stays).
.BR tui_sgrview_handle ()
returns 1 when the key was a scrolling key, else 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tui_textview_init (3),
.BR tui_mdview_init (3),
.BR tui_canvas_of (3),
.BR libtuikit (7)
